FINAL ANSWER:
The two main owners are **Troy Goode** (about 40% of the lines still in the repo) and **Douglas Christopher Wilson** (about 32%). Troy owns most of the library code itself.

Plain `git blame` gives a misleading answer here. It credits **Fiona Formatter** with 1016 of 1995 surviving lines (51%), but all of those come from commit `62628c0`, which only changed indentation and quotes. Commit `b2005d9` (Troy, laptop email) only added `// checked` comments to 12 existing lines. I ignored both commits and attributed each line to the person who wrote its logic. I also counted Troy's two email addresses as one person.

**Surviving lines by author (1995 tracked lines):**

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 808 | 40.5% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | 31.5% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 4.8% |
| Jon Church | 72 | 3.6% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3.4% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | 2.6% |
| Others (long tail) | ~270 | ~14% |

**By area:**
- **`lib/index.js` (238 lines):** Troy wrote 157 lines (66%). Doug has 22 and Alejandro Caravaca Puchades has 16. Troy is effectively the only owner of the runtime code.
- **`test/` (966 lines):** Troy has 517 (54%) and Doug has 374 (39%). This area is shared between the two.
- **`README.md`:** Troy has 116 lines and Jon Church has 72.
- **`HISTORY.md`:** Mostly Doug (50 lines).
- **`.github/workflows/`:** Íñigo Marquínez Prado wrote 95 lines of CI config (ci, scorecard) and Sebastian Beltran wrote 63 (codeql).

By commit count Doug leads (143 commits against Troy's 120). By surviving code, Troy is ahead, especially in `lib/`. The bus-factor risk is in `lib/`, because nearly all of it depends on one person.

To make plain `git blame` give this answer too, add a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file listing `62628c0` and `b2005d9`. Then run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`. GitHub's blame view also reads that file. Tell me if you want it.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log --format='%h %an <%ae> %ad %s' --date=short -8 && git ls-files | head -50 && git ls-files | wc -l && git show --stat 62628c0 b2005d9 02afce3 | head -60
 - Bash: git show b2005d9 | head -60; git show 62628c0 -w --stat | tail -3; ls -a; git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
 - Bash: blame(){ for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --line-porcelain "$@" -- "$f" | sed -n 's/^author //p'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8; echo ---; }; echo NAIVE; blame; echo IGNORE_FMT_AND_ANNOT; blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9; echo "CODE ONLY (lib+test), same ignores"; for f in $(git ls-files lib test | grep '\.js$'); do git blame --line-porcelain -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 -- "$f" | sed -n 's/^author //p'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8; echo; echo "lib/index.js only"; git blame --line-porcelain -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 -- lib/index.js | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
 - Bash: git ls-files | xargs cat | wc -l; git ls-files lib test | grep '\.js$' | xargs cat | wc -l; for f in README.md HISTORY.md; do echo $f; git blame --line-porcelain -w -M -C -- $f | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3; done
FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode owns most of the code still in the repo. Douglas Christopher Wilson is a clear second. A plain `git blame` gives a misleading answer, because two recent commits rewrote lines without changing what they do.

**Why plain blame is wrong here**
- `62628c0` by Fiona Formatter (2026-04-12) only reformatted the files: 4-space indent and double quotes. It touched 1016 lines, so plain blame credits her with 1016 of 1993 lines. She wrote none of that logic. `-w` doesn't fix this, because changing quotes is more than a whitespace change.
- `b2005d9` by Troy (`troy@laptop.example`) only added `// checked` comments to 12 lines in `lib/index.js`.
- I re-ran blame with `--ignore-rev` for both commits, plus `-w -M -C` so lines that were moved or copied keep their original author. Troy's two emails count as one person, and so do `alex94puchades` and Alejandro Caravaca Puchades.

**Who wrote the surviving lines**

| Scope | Troy Goode | Douglas C. Wilson | Next |
|---|---|---|---|
| Whole repo (1993 lines) | 808 (~41%) | 629 (~32%) | Íñigo Marquínez Prado 95, Jon Church 72 |
| JS code in `lib/` + `test/` (1202) | 674 (~56%) | 394 (~33%) | Alejandro Caravaca Puchades 30 |
| `lib/index.js`, the actual library (238) | 157 (~66%) | 22 (~9%) | Alejandro 16, Raymond Feng 9 |

- **Troy** wrote most of the library logic and most of `README.md` (116 lines).
- **Douglas** has the most commits (143 against Troy's 120). His surviving lines are mostly tests and `HISTORY.md`, and he has little left in `lib/index.js`.
- The other contributors each have small, scattered pieces. Much of what Íñigo, Jon Church, Sebastian Beltran and Ulises Gascón still have is CI/workflow config and README text, not library code.

The ownership I'm describing is authorship of surviving lines, not who knows the code best today.

To see these numbers in normal `git blame` output, put `62628c0` and `b2005d9` in a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file and run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`. GitHub's blame view also reads that file.

